# xkbcomp -- the keymap compiler the X server SHELLS OUT TO, and the clearest
# instance in this tree of finding 10: a decoder that nothing at build time
# checks for.
#
# Xwayland does not link this. It builds a command line and runs it
# (xkb/ddxLoad.c 154-176):
#
#     "<bindir>/xkbcomp" -w 1 "-R<xkbdir>" -xkm "-" ... "<outdir>/server-:0.xkm"
#
# writes the keymap description into that process's stdin, and reads the .xkm
# back. So xkbcomp's absence is invisible to every build check there is:
# Xwayland compiles, links, installs and starts. What happens instead is
# Popen() failing at the first keymap load, one line in the log --
# "XKB: Could not invoke xkbcomp" -- and an X11 session whose keyboard does
# nothing. That reads as a compositor bug, not a missing package, which is why
# it is declared as the runtime dependency it is rather than left to the
# distribution to remember.
#
# THE SECOND HALF OF THE SAME FACT: the keymap DATA is xkeyboard-config, which
# this package resolves at runtime through -R<xkbdir>. It is declared below for
# the same reason -- xkbcomp with no rules directory fails at exactly the same
# moment, in exactly the same way.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://www.x.org/pub/individual/app/xkbcomp-1.4.7.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=0a288114e5f44e31987042c79aecff1ffad53a8154b8ec971c24a69a80f81f77
SRC_DIR=xkbcomp-1.4.7

# --with-xkb-config-root IS STATED RATHER THAN DEFAULTED, and the default is
# '${datadir}/X11/xkb' (configure.ac 67-71) -- a substitution, resolved from
# --prefix, baked into the binary as DFLT_XKB_CONFIG_ROOT and ALSO published in
# xkbcomp.pc as xkbconfigdir.
#
# That second use is what makes it worth writing out: xwayland's meson reads
# xkbconfigdir back out of this .pc to decide its own XKB_BASE_DIRECTORY
# (meson.build 116-123). So this string is the agreement between three packages
# -- xkeyboard-config installs there, xkbcomp defaults to it, and Xwayland
# passes it back to xkbcomp with -R. It is the same literal xkeyboard-config's
# recipe pins with -Dxkb-base, and the two must not drift.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--with-xkb-config-root=/usr/share/X11/xkb"
